    "updated_at": "2024-09-10T14:51:59Z",
    "body": "> So, should we replicate similar text in a bunch of places, or define it somewhere central and then reference it?\r\n\r\nMy thought was to have some default behavior for non-style rule cases, either disallowing relative length units entirely, or using some default values (though what default values you would use for the viewport for cases that might not have access to a viewport, like some of the HTML canvas color parsing functions, is unclear).\r\n\r\n(as I forgot to cc the relevant editors originally, doing that now, @tabatkins @fantasai). ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
