    "body": "<details>\r\n  <summary><strong><i>edit:</i></strong> sorry, this comment was not useful because resolving relative lengths based on computed values is wrong, and the <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/mediaqueries-5/#units\">spec</a> is already clear for media queries.</summary>\r\n\r\nI think they always resolve based on the computed values of the root element but it might be useful to clarify it, especially for nested `@media`. Consequently and to complete your list, it could be clarified for `@import`, which accepts a `<media-query-list>` in its prelude.\r\n</details>",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
