    "updated_at": "2026-07-08T16:24:18Z",
    "body": "Sorry for missing this for so long! God, I get too many emails.\n\nYes, I agree with @emilio in this regard. The big contextual thing is \"have an element to resolve against\", and I think we can define that category pretty generally. Specific things like `@font-face`/etc just need to define how they're obtaining their non-obvious element reference.\n\nIf there *are* any cases that dont' have an element reference but *do* still have some way to resolve these types of things they'll need more specifics, yeah.",
