    "created_at": "2026-07-08T16:32:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-08T16:32:17Z",
    "body": "The CSS Working Group just discussed `[css-values] Specs that use CSS values outside of normal style rules should provide information on calc()/non-absolute length resolution in a uniform way`.\n\n<details><summary>The full IRC log of that discussion</summary>\n&lt;ydaniv> weinig: the gist is that going through the specs and impl. on WebKit, there are some places outside normal resolution, where styles need to be resolved in some way<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... the spec doesn't give guidance on how to do that<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... like DOM APIs for animations, but also places like Media Quereis<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... and also now includes canvas, where it refrences colors, etc.<br>\n&lt;TabAtkins> q+<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... so authors should be able to clearly define the rules for parsing, but it's currently not standaridised<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack ydaniv<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack TabAtkins<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> TabAtkins: just posted to the issue, I agree whith what emilio said there<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... usually you have an element for reference, and should be easy to define<br>\n&lt;emilio> q+<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... if there are places without an element or reference, I strongly agree with saying, we need a ref, if you don't have one, you can not resolve<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... need to define wehter it's parse error, or should have a default<br>\n&lt;fantasai> +1 to considering it an error, unless we define otherwise<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> weinig: in addition to the element, there's a question about if element ref is not available, should root stuff be supported? Or if view-relative units be supported, etc.<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... in generally I support it<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> TabAtkins: yea, Media queries should fallback to root, but let's do it<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> weinig: I can categorize it and put it into the bug<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack emilio<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> emilio: wanted also to define it.<br>\n&lt;astearns> s/it./when/<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... if we want to allow font units relative to root then we need to decide if those gets resolved as [missed]<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> ... if we can get away with has element ref or not, seems fine<br>\n&lt;fantasai> Emilio's point is that for e.g. IntersectionObserver, do we define that the units resolve when you set the callback, or each time the intersection is evaluated<br>\n&lt;fantasai> So need to define not just what we resolve against, but when<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> weinig: any text we do add to the spec we should indicate what's the requirements, when style resolution should work immediately? or not? is there an invalidation loop? is it persistent?<br>\n&lt;astearns> ack fantasai<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> fantasai: I support clarifying these. good idea. I think that making things invalid is also a way to go, where if we know what to do later we can apply it<br>\n&lt;kbabbitt> +1<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> astearns: sounds like we agree about the way forward and weinig is going to add cases to the issue<br>\n&lt;ydaniv> weinig: I'll make a big table<br>\n</details>\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
